{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/7/codegen_prompts/2.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/7`\n- 题号：`2`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/7/2.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"2\">\n- `description`：用种子色块的形状作为印章，沿连接线路径在每个中继节点处盖印，印章颜色由该节点自身的颜色决定。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干个小型实心彩色色块（3×3 以内），称为\"种子\"；每个种子颜色唯一，且种子的形状各不相同（例如一个 L 形、一个 T 形、一个直线段等）。\n  - 另有若干单像素的\"中继节点\"，每个中继节点有自己的颜色（可以是 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow、Magenta 等），且该颜色不与任何种子的颜色相同。\n  - Grey 像素构成一像素宽的直线段\"连接线\"，每条连接线连接恰好一个种子与一个或多个中继节点（Grey 线与种子边缘及中继节点 4-连通相邻）。\n  - 每个中继节点通过连接线只与一个种子相连。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：沿 Grey 连接线追踪，确定每个中继节点所属的种子。\n  - 第二步：取该种子的形状（像素相对位置模式）作为印章模板。\n  - 第三步：以中继节点所在像素为印章的左上角，用中继节点自身的颜色绘制该印章形状。绘制时，若印章像素超出网格边界则裁剪，若印章像素覆盖到 Grey 连接线则覆盖之。\n  - 种子本身保持不变，连接线中未被覆盖的 Grey 像素也保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：形状来自种子（通过连接线追踪获得），颜色来自中继节点自身——解题者必须分别识别\"形状从哪来\"和\"颜色从哪来\"这两条独立的信息通道。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/e87109e9, train/aa62e3f4, train/e39e9282, train/db7260a4, eval/a251c730, train/652646ff, train/5adee1b2, train/e9fc42f2\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"e87109e9\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4200\nmechanism=0.4809\nlexical=0.0152\ncode_feature=0.7500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:path, object:sprite, object:template, operation:crop_resize, output:crop, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e87109e9.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e87109e9.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nEmit four teal beams from a square, turning at colored obstacles per a legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- Top band: grey (5) legend with colored vertical bars in cells; bar position (left or right) encodes turn direction.\n- Below: main grid with bg, a solid teal (8) square, and colored obstacle blocks.\n\nRule:\n- Remove the legend from the output.\n- From the teal square, shoot a beam in each cardinal direction (as a sliding copy of the square).\n- Each beam paints teal over bg cells as it moves.\n- On hitting an obstacle of color C, consult the legend: bar on left → turn counterclockwise, bar on right → turn clockwise. Continue in the new direction.\n- Beams stop at grid edges.\n\nKey insight: The legend's bar position (left vs right within its cell) is the encoding for turn direction at each obstacle color.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Isolated teal square emits lines in four directions, turning on obstacle contact based on legend color bar position.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"isolated teal square s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"extend in 4 cardinal directions; on hitting obstacle, turn counterclockwise if legend shows same-color bar on left, clockwise if on right\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint teal along path until obstacle or grid edge\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend entries: obstacle_color with bar on left → counterclockwise turn; bar on right → clockwise turn\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"tight crop\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"turning-rules\",\n    \"legend-interpretation\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\",\n  \"type2\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src2\": \"grey legend region at top s\",\n  \"dst2\": \"\",\n  \"match_cond2\": \"\",\n  \"path2\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory2\": \"\",\n  \"transform2\": \"remove from output\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aa62e3f4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3365\nmechanism=0.4022\nlexical=0.0147\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aa62e3f4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/aa62e3f4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace the outlined object with the outside contour of that outline in the marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background surrounds one 8-connected foreground outline.\n- The outline is the unique largest foreground color.\n- One or more smaller interior colors are inside the outline; the marker color\n  is the unique smallest non-outline color.\n\nRule:\n- Erase all original foreground pixels to background.\n- Paint every background pixel that is 4-adjacent to the outline with the\n  marker color.\n- Keep the grid shape unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The colored interior marker supplies the paint color, while the\nlargest outline supplies only the contour whose outside edge is traced.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one 8-connected largest foreground outline object and smaller interior marker colors on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase all original foreground pixels; repaint the background pixels 4-adjacent to the outline with the unique smallest non-outline marker color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e39e9282\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3475\nmechanism=0.3738\nlexical=0.0169\ncode_feature=0.7500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:sprite, relation:adjacent, relation:inside, relation:overlap\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e39e9282.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e39e9282.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nProject maroon markers into adjacent grey or pink 3x3 squares, erasing grey squares afterward.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background, solid 3x3 grey and/or pink squares, and maroon marker pixels or segments directly touching one side of exactly one square.\nRule\nGrey squares are erased; their adjacent maroon markers stay in place and stamp the nearest edge cell inside the grey square. Pink squares stay pink; their adjacent maroon markers disappear and stamp the corresponding cell on the square's middle row or middle column.\nKey insight\nThe side touched by a marker determines the projection: grey uses the near edge, while pink uses the centerline, preserving the marker's coordinate along that side.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"maroon marker pixels or segments adjacent to solid grey or pink 3x3 square objects\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase grey squares after stamping maroon into each touched near-edge cell; keep grey-adjacent markers in place; keep pink squares, remove pink-adjacent markers, and stamp their maroon cells onto the matching middle row or column of the pink square\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"db7260a4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3646\nmechanism=0.3991\nlexical=0.0159\ncode_feature=0.7500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:path, object:sprite, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/db7260a4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/db7260a4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop the singleton marker into the matching red U-shaped container, or make a bottom-row puddle if no closed container is hit.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background, one singleton marker pixel on the top row,\n  and one other foreground color forming vertical bars and bottom segments.\n- A closed container is a U shape: two vertical side bars with a continuous\n  bottom segment between them and an empty rectangular interior above the bottom.\n\nRule\n- Remove the top marker from its original cell.\n- If exactly one closed U-shaped container has the marker column within its\n  horizontal footprint, fill that container's empty interior with the marker color.\n- If no closed container is under the marker column, fill the whole bottom row\n  with the marker color.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker does not identify a color by value; it identifies a vertical drop\n  column, and only a structurally closed U shape can catch and contain the fill.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"singleton top-row marker pixel\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical drop down the marker column; a closed U-shaped wall container catches the drop when the marker column lies within its horizontal footprint, otherwise the path reaches the bottom edge\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed U-shaped container interior, or the bottom row if no closed container catches the drop\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill the caught container's background interior with the marker color; if uncaught, fill the whole bottom row\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase the original marker pixel and keep all wall pixels unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a251c730\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3207\nmechanism=0.3791\nlexical=0.0143\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:marker, object:sprite, object:template, operation:crop_resize, output:crop, relation:inside, relation:overlap\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a251c730.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/a251c730.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nStamp source sprites into a destination frame via color-matched singleton markers.\n\nInput structure:\n- Two bordered rectangles: source (multi-cell sprites) and destination (singleton markers).\n- Each sprite has an anchor pixel — its least-frequent color. Markers share these colors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each destination marker to the source sprite with the same anchor color.\n- Translate the sprite so its anchor overlaps the marker position.\n- Output is the destination rectangle, interior cleared before stamping.\n\nKey insight: The rarest color per sprite doubles as a template key and positioning anchor.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"sprite s with anchor pixel inside the source framed rectangle\",\n  \"dst\": \"anchored on singleton marker pixel d inside the destination framed rectangle\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.anchor_color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"overlap s.anchor with d\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to only retain the destination rectangle\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"652646ff\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3472\nmechanism=0.4187\nlexical=0.0127\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, object:template, operation:crop_resize, output:crop, relation:direction, relation:overlap\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/652646ff.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/652646ff.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecover each partially hidden 6x6 ring sprite and stack complete copies from top layer to bottom layer.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
